{"contents":"The third requirement is not as easy to verify as the first two, so we will also give an equivalent infinitesimal definition from which the Poisson distribution falls out via approximation to the binomial distribution.

{% proof %}
Call the two definitions  D1 and D2. 
We will show that D1(2, 3, 4) implies D2(3).
Let $T_1$ be the first arrival time and denote $p_t(k):=\Prob(N(t)=k)$. Then D1(3) implies:
$$
\lim_{t \to 0} \frac{p_t(1)}{t} = \lambda. \tag{3}
$$
From D1(1) we have $p_0(1) = 0$.

